            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Is there any alternative here where we leverage phosphor-state-manager dependencies to make it so obmc-console doesn't start before the card is powered on?\n\nI don't think that \"unplugged\" vs \"plugged\" solves 100% of the problem described in the rest of the commit message.  If we have the BIC powered off, is there a similar issue with the hardware not providing the UART?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Sean He",
                        "email": "sean.he.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Dsean0212"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @patrick@stwcx.xyz,\nThank you for your helpful feedback. I implemented the hotplug and power\u2011control fixes by adding a dependency for the obmc-console service in an alternative commit:\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/openbmc/+/86809 \nCould you please review that commit and continue the discussion there? I\u2019m happy to address any further comments or make adjustments as needed.\n\nThanks again for the review!"
                },
